  "body": "Red in a full `go test -timeout 45m ./...` on mote (macOS 27, load ~65-70 from other sessions' runs) at 9d0c9b41e (v0.1.2977):\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestAuthLockWaitDoesNotFreezeTheHost (0.44s)\n    auth_lock_async_test.go:29: exit status 1\n        AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: a timer on the same loop kept running while changeAuth waited for the lock: 7 ticks\n            at [eval]:33:10\nFAIL\tgithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/plugin\t229.760s\n```\n\nThe test (7aff42d86, #5112) counts a 20ms setInterval over a 300ms sleep and wants >= 8 ticks (15 ideal). On a loaded machine a timer that fires late counts fewer ticks while the loop is free all the same, so this measures the scheduler, not the freeze it is named for. A frozen loop (the Atomics.wait it guards against) gives 0-1 ticks over the 600ms hold, so a bound like \">= 2\" or a check that the timer ran at all while the lock is held keeps the guarantee with room under load (\"a timing test leaves room on both sides\", code standards).\n\nNot my change's package (that was internal/cli, internal/gui, internal/proc); not rerun alone.\n",
